      "side": 1,
      "message": "Dear Greg,\n\nA vendor hook for workqueue watchdog timer has been applied at Bug 169374262.\nWe\u0027ll print out several logs including information of a runqueue owned by pool-\u003ecpu.\nThis log message help us analyzing a workqueue lockup problem.\n\npr_info(\"CPU%u [CFS util_avg:%lu load_avg:%lu nr_running:%u][RT rt_nr_running:%u][avg_rt util_avg:%lu]\\n\",\n\tcpu, cpu_rq(cpu)-\u003ecfs.avg.util_avg, cpu_rq(cpu)-\u003ecfs.avg.load_avg, cpu_rq(cpu)-\u003ecfs.nr_running,\n\tcpu_rq(cpu)-\u003ert.rt_nr_running, cpu_rq(cpu)-\u003eavg_rt.util_avg);\n\nExample)\n[  646.111602] BUG: workqueue lockup - pool cpus\u003d0 node\u003d0 flags\u003d0x0 nice\u003d0 stuck for 57s!\n[  646.111721] CPU0 [CFS util_avg:1023 load_avg:2047 nr_running:2][RT util_avg:0][avg_rt util_avg:0]   \u003c-----------------!!",
